          <p>
            Two notes on the Gold Standard column. Optimum Nutrition's own product page shows the supplement facts only as an image, but it confirms the 24 g of protein and 5.5 g of BCAAs per scoop. Some grocery listings still show an older panel with a 30.4 g scoop and 50 mg of sodium, so the tub in your hand may differ slightly by lot. ON does not publish a leucine figure, so we cannot compare the two on the amino acid that matters most for muscle protein synthesis.
          </p>

          <p>
            On the Naked side, the 2.98 g of leucine and the 5.87 g of BCAAs come from the amino profile Naked prints on its own label image (isoleucine 1,491 mg, leucine 2,982 mg, valine 1,395 mg). Naked also sells 2 lb ($62.99) and 1 lb ($37.99) bags; we did not record their serving counts, so the cost-per-gram figures here use the 5 lb bag only.
          </p>
